course: dictionary
lesson: 2752
title: Feeling let down
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: When something you hoped for does not happen, you feel disappointed. «Zara felt a little disappointed» when she got a gift card for a game she does not even play. The word tells you her hope did not come true, even though she still thanked her uncle.
explain: Disappointed is an adjective, so it describes a feeling: a disappointed face, or a disappointed child. Its verb form is disappoint, which means to make someone feel this way. «The film disappointed me» means the film was not as good as I expected.
explain: Look for clues around the word. In «she's gutted (very disappointed)», the words in brackets tell you the meaning. Gutted is British slang, so people say it in different ways, but disappointed is the word you will see in books and at school.
fact: Disappointed means sad because something you hoped for did not happen, or was not as good as you expected.
fact: «Disappointed» can be followed by in, with or that: «disappointed in someone», «disappointed with something», «disappointed that…».
fact: More disappointed and most disappointed are the comparison forms.
fact: «Gutted» is British slang for very disappointed.
fact: Disappointed is also the past form of the verb disappoint, as in «the film disappointed me».
exercise: «Zara felt a little disappointed when she got a gift card for a game she does not even play.» What does disappointed mean here? | Tired after a long day | *Sad because her hope did not come true | Very excited and happy | Angry with her uncle
exercise: «The film disappointed me.» Here disappointed is a verb form. What does it mean? | Made me feel very sleepy | Showed me a new place | *Made me feel sad because it was not as good as I expected | Made me laugh a lot
exercise: «She was disappointed that the match was cancelled.» Which word is British slang that means very disappointed? | smashing | *gutted | hurl | legend
test: «Then she misses her mate's party because she has to mind the boys, and she's gutted.» Which word is closest in meaning to gutted? | Pleased | Bored with the game | Very hungry | *Very disappointed
test: Which form is the past of disappoint? | *disappointed | disappointment | disappointing | disappoints
exam: Sam was ___ that the match was cancelled, so he sat by the window waiting for news. | *disappointed | smashing | legend | hurl
